' ============================================================================
' 44 The Ziv loop of a correctly rounded function.
'
' Source of Figure TL9 in ../tensor-logic/dynamic-semantics.md (section 3.3).
' The figure restates CR of that section (Ziv 1991). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. The exact cases return their rounding at once, with no loop.
'   2. Each round encloses f(x) in a rigorous dyadic interval at the working
'      width w. Decision 89 removed the reservation of each round.
'   3. If both ends round to one p-bit value, that value is RN_p(f(x)).
'   4. Otherwise the width doubles, up to the cap 4p + 128. An input that the
'      cap cannot decide fails with PrecisionExhausted.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 44-tl-ziv-loop.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 44-tl-ziv-loop
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam PartitionBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title The Ziv loop: CR(f, x, p)

start
:a CR function f, an exact input x,
and the precision p in [8, 256]; <<$rrs_tl_term>>
if (an exact case? for example <latex>e^{0} = 1</latex> or <latex>\sigma(0) = 1/2</latex>) then (yes)
  :return <latex>\mathrm{RN}_p(\mathrm{exact}(f, x))</latex>; <<$rrs_effect>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
:<latex>w \leftarrow p + 32</latex> (32 guard bits); <<$rrs_tl_engine>>
repeat
  ' Changed by decision 89: the node has no host-work budget, so a round reserves nothing. The text before:
  ' :reserve STEP-COST(f, x, w) on the meter
  ' (decision 40: reserve before the work); <<$rrs_meter>>
  ' if (the reservation fits the budget?) then (no)
  '   :HostWorkRejected; <<$rrs_reject>>
  '   stop
  ' else (yes)
  ' endif
  :enclose: <latex>[lo, hi] \ni f(x)</latex>, a rigorous dyadic
  interval at the working width w; <<$rrs_tl_engine>>
  if (<latex>\mathrm{RN}_p(lo) = \mathrm{RN}_p(hi)</latex>?) then (yes)
    :return <latex>\mathrm{RN}_p(lo) = \mathrm{RN}_p(f(x))</latex>
    (the rounding is monotone); <<$rrs_effect>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
  if (<latex>w = 4p + 128</latex>?) then (yes)
    :PrecisionExhausted; <<$rrs_reject>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
  :<latex>w \leftarrow \min(2w, 4p + 128)</latex>
  (for p = 64: 96, 192, 384); <<$rrs_tl_engine>>
repeat while (next round)

' Changed by decision 89: the node has no host-work meter, so the legend has no meter row. The row before:
' |<$rrs_meter>     | a reservation on the host-work meter |
legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_tl_term>   | the input |
|<$rrs_tl_engine> | a step of the loop |
|<$rrs_effect>    | the correctly rounded result |
|<$rrs_reject>    | a typed failure |
endlegend
@enduml
